=== TITLE: USG Early Pregnancy / 1st Trimester Viability ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
SINGLE LIVE INTRAUTERINE GESTATION CORRESPONDING TO 7 WEEKS 4 DAYS WITH NORMAL CARDIAC ACTIVITY.
- No subchorionic hematoma or adnexal pathology.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: ULTRASONOGRAPHY FOR EARLY PREGNANCY (TRANSABDOMINAL & TVS)

CLINICAL INDICATION: Confirmation of pregnancy and gestational age assessment.

OBSERVATIONS:
- Uterus: Enlarged, gravido-anteverted with good decidual reaction.
- Gestational Sac (GS): Single, regular, well-defined intrauterine gestational sac visualized measuring 24.5 mm (Corresponds to 7 Weeks 3 Days).
- Yolk Sac: Visualized, round, regular, measuring 4.2 mm.
- Embryo / Foetal Pole: Single foetal pole identified within the gestational sac.
- Crown-Rump Length (CRL): Measures 13.2 mm (Corresponds to 7 Weeks 4 Days).
- Cardiac Activity: Visualized clearly, regular foetal heart rate of 148 bpm with regular rhythm.
- Choriodecidual Reaction: Adequate and homogeneous. No subchorionic hematoma or retroplacental collection seen.
- Internal Os: Closed. Cervical canal length is adequate (3.6 cm).
- Adnexa: Right ovary demonstrates a normal Corpus Luteum cyst (18 mm). Both adnexa appear free.